        <p>111 BAKERS' MAIN.</p>
        <p>The annuli distribution rol prism In connection with the bowling rosin of the Warrington branch of the Amalgamated Union of Operative Bikers and Conroe- Boosts was held et the Blue Bell lea on Saturday evening. Mr. Eakereley, president of the blaster Bakers' Association, made the distribution. Mr. Oita car, in proposing a vote of thanks to the d onots of the prizes, said the master bakers had given largely to the prim fund, and that showed the good spirit which existed between the roasters eel the men. Mr. EATON seconded and the proposition was unani- mously carried. A vote of thanks was accorded to Mr. Eokersley, on the proposition of Mr. RATHBONE, INCOII en by Mr. REMIT. Me. EcK RSLE V, in reply, mid there was a gent difference between the baker of lbn present day and the baker of thirty years ago, and he thought the Improve- ment was largely doe to the Aroslgsmated Union. (Applause). The prise-winners were.. follow :-1, W l'endleton ; 2, C F Eaten ; 3, .1 Bste ; 4, W Rathimue. main : 1, T Bathroom. ; 2, F Everett.</p>
