        <head>WARRINGTON BRIDGE DELAY.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON BRIDGE DELAY.</p>
        <p>"SOMETHING DRASTIC SHOULD BE DONE.'</p>
        <p>What About the Howley Scheme'</p>
        <p>The evergreen topic of the new bridges schemes tvs4 again brought forward at the meeting of the Warring- ton Town Council on Tuesday evening. It was reported that at • meeting of the Bridges Commit). the Town Clerk submitted the draft contract with Messrs. Alfred Thorne and Sons' and explained the alter.tions which bad been made therein, and the result of en in'erview with the contractors at which were present the Chair- men, Deputy Chairman and Councillor Wilkinson. It wee resolved that the draft contemn as settled with the contractor' be approved. Alderman So ETRURST moved the confirmation of the otioutee, end said he should base done no with greater plea..n if they could only pt to wotk. (Hear, lies, Ile had been on a holiday, and if he had not been away he did not know what he should have done during the past two or three weeks. (Laughter.) Something ought to be done of a drastic character to pus't matters forward. He felt very stronely shoot the proposed bridge at Howley. (Hear, hear.) Now that the Corporation Bill had been pasetd they ought not to lose a moment's time, hut get the plans out. It was understood that when the Bill had been got through a valuation of certain land would be tondo, the money deposited In the bank And the bridge commenced. He could not hear of anything being done yet, lot he hoped It would not be much longer delayed. It was getting nearly as bad an Warrington Bridge—the work hanging and nothing being done. The Mt von seconded the motion for the pawing of the minutes and said everything was bring done that could be done with reference to building the new War- rington Bridge. The worthy aldermen had been away for. holiday and was very keen on work. (Laughter.) Councillor CuSNTLER —What progrerw Las been made about Howley llrirl.e')) Councillor ISEL LI AN asked if the erection of the two bridgea was in the hands of the Bridget) Committee. It wee his impression that the committee was formed simply to carry out the construction of )Varrington Bridge ? Aldermen SI ETU MIST.— Oh no ! I Councillor Bottles. Are they going to have complete °entre! over Howley Bridge? The MAYOR it is plum!. Councillor JACKSON HOLNIIIS wee planed Aldermen Smethurst bsd not entirely forgotten Howley Bridge. He should like to have some information through the Deputy Town Clerk as to the Pact position of effairs. The DEPUTY TOWN CLERK said the special Bridges Committee bad been appointed solely for the construc- tion of Warrington Midge. Councillor Ilittmeat : I thought no. I The Dgrury Town CLERK t It is for the Commit' to decide what they shell do with Howley Bridge-- whether they shall hand over the work to the Bridges Committee or to the General Purposes Committee. It is impoesible to start the building of Howley Bridge at present on account of legal diffloultim, but theee are . being attended to and powiltly in sin months you may see Howley Bridge tm. (Hear, hem.) I estimate it will be up in time to go to the new bowling glee, Mr. Lowlife is in communication with the contrecters with regard to the amended imamate, because the first eetimate was given for a different portion of the river than that over which the bridge is going to be placed. lean assure the Council thet every step is being taken to hurry on the work as quickly as possible. (ilear,heer, Councillor An HICH. was glad to hear Alderman Smethurst introducing the question of the necessity for • commencement being made with the work of the ooustroction of /fowley Bridge. People in that ward, , of which he was a representative, were /Milo. for the work to he taken in hand and completed as soon ne possible. Then were beginning to talk of the dilatori- nets of the Bridge. Committee. Ile would be obliged) if they would push the matter forward r la. all possible speed. Councillor ROBERTS said thet according to thee Deputy Town Clerk there was no Howley Bridge Com- mittee at all and therefore if anyone wee to blame, it. was the Town Connell. The DEPUTY TOWN CLERK mild tint perhaps the reason why the epeclel committee was called the. o Bridges Committee" eras because it was pulling down one bridge and petting up another. (Laughter ) Alderman TINNION said too muck time was spent is talking about the bridges. It wee time they got on with the werk. (Hear, bear.) The mioutes were approved. THE CONTRACT. WHO SHALL DRIVE PILES ?</p>
