        <p>The Mono. moved That the draft contrut with Messrs. Alfred Thorne and Sons for the c Instruction of the Warrington Bridge and training wells, now submitted by the Town Clerk, he approved, and that the common meal of the Corpuration be Mated thereto?' Alderumn Siif 11,E mounded and the proposition was agreed to. Alderman Pi ER I.OIN r asked whether before the heat arrangements wero completed the Council could use Its influence wit the Bridges Committee t, alTord an opportunity to the I) .potv.hl iyor to be essociated with the Mayor mud Alderman Smethurst in the. ceremony of pile driving. It was largely through Alderman Furshee's strenuous eff wets that the Council at length decided in (aeon, of an ttO ft. bridge. ,Tb. Moron promised to introduce the matter and eupport it at the Bridges Committee, ash, had done before. Both he end A Idet man Smethont supported it, bet the majority wiled twined it. Alderman PiErtpoirr : Sometimes second thoughts are hest. Aldermen Torsion : Are we in order in discussing the matter ? The DEVOTE Town CLERK: No, SIE.</p>
