      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-05_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>WARRINGTON CHILDREN'S CAMP.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON CHILDREN'S CAMP.</p>
        <p>The second belch of girls numbering one hundred and' twenty under the cure of Mr. Todd arrived at Preatatyn ,on Saturdsy morning where they were met by the Mimes Ellison, Behhingtor. Davenport, Posey, Ernson, land Mrs. Burge, who have taken °large of them during the week. I bey merchel to the camp and were placed in motion. for the Carioca hut.. Dinner was served and wee greatly enjoyed. Afterwards the children played game. In the field. Tney then had ten awl pre- pered their beds for the night. On Sunday the children were eerly astir after the usual naorninin orb the Ronne Catholic ails were taken to church at Crestetyn. Tan Church of Enghand section joined the children of Melidnn ia a speeiel service in the afternoon. 'lie evening 1,1131 spent on the abore. On Monday morning the children walks I along the shore to eon the pierrots. Toe afternoon ant evening were spent on the shore. On Tuesday the weather was very unsettled so the. day mu ;mentor, the shire and clasp ground various. games being Indulged In. On Werinesosy morning the children were taken to see the bnnotifol wtterfall at Dyserth the return journey being msde through the wools on the moun- tain side. All were quite ready for ringer when they reached hnme. On Thursday morning the children were taken firs ramble through the nut g ovas on the mnuntain side, returning via Meliden. Friday was a very bury day, tbe girl. Irsisted in pre- paring assaults for the b iya who will arrive ti.day. The children have spent a very happy holiday. The wing which hue been erected this season has hem very mach appreciated.</p>
      </div>
