        <p>The Liberals of Warrington have held many great open-air ineetinge during the pact few year., but all previous recor•ls were broken on Saturday evening when a crowd lat least 5,0{01 assembled to celebrate the opening of the handsome new lecture van which the Liberal Association his purchased to facilitate is propaganda work. Remarkable enthusiasm characterised the proceedings and the unanimity with which a resolution of confidence in the Government was carried showed how completely progressive legislation in commending itself to the workers. The arrival of Mr. an I Me. A. H. Cr.,stield was the signal for • splendid ovation, the huge audience cheering , them for several minutes. There were many expressions of admiration for the new van, which could not be better adapted for the purpose of open- sir campaigning. Mr. C. E. Pauker , president of the Liberal Association) presided and amongst others present were: -Mr snd Mrs A 11 Crosfield, Alderman Pierpoint, Councillors J Wilkinson. .I'l' Locker and J Hawthorn, Mrs Osborne, Mr and Mrs P Delaney, Mrs Walker, Miss Walker, Mrs New, Rev W Cooper, T Pemberon, J (.1 Withinshaw, P Peacock, .1 Jarman,J Worrell, M I lowar.h, It Farrar. ItT Rushton Joseph Wilkinson, II New, and I.: A Sanders.</p>
