        <p>.„ . then they broke, and l•ft my forehead very red. Next they would dry up and the scales would come off my forehea 1 like those if a fish. My face, nose and shoulders were very red, and the skin peeled off my brow and forehead. I could get no rod. Igm a great many ointments from druggists and doctoia, but nothil g would cure Ine except the Cuticura Remedies. I got two boxes of Cuticura Ointment and one cake of Cuticura Soap. They were enough to cure me, and to get rid of every ap,t. My skin is quite clear now. " I am no thankful to ace the mune of Cuticura , Ointment and I recommend it to every suffever. I say it is the greatest Ointment on the market, for old or young, and all families might to keep it in the house. It is woith a pound a box to any sufferer from skin ditiesses " ,Signedi Richard Trevers, flocking. Court, Redruth, Cornwall, July 26, 1910. Post free, from F. Newbery ,k Sons, 27, Charterhotme , London, samples of Cuticura Soap and Ointment, with 32-p. Inook on skin treatment.</p>
