        <p>I,IIIIN, F. IN ONE F NMI! VI FOR. 100 V6AIIN.—Mr. Steel applied for temporary authority for Mr. harry liertham. Liverpool-rest, Warrington, to tell at the Ferry Inn, Penketh, in place of Miss Johnson. Mr. Steel pointed out that the licence had been in the Johnson family for 100 years. The late Mr. Johnson I died about two years ago and the licence wan taken over by his daughter, mho was 0911 retiring. Notice had been given for the application to he made to the Newton Justices on Thureday next for the transfer of the licence to Mr. lierthanc—Mr. White The licence is passing nut t f the family ill ! Mr. Steel Yen I sir. alter 100 yearn.—The application aria granted. UNRE015,111.1,10 CANAL BOAT.—Enmet. Croydon, 15, Fenwick.street, Liverpool, wen fined St. it, and coats for bAng the owner of the canal lost" Jesaie, 'the acme ring use.l are l,vellingb'roawtltoret being registered.</p>
