        <p>The Rev. Willisos Arthur Beckett, who boo inen eppuinted superintendent minister of the Wevrington %Vetsleynn Circuit, his hal • eidit experience of active work in Methodism. His ministry covers about :10 years, the lest six of n Lich have beeo vent in L'indon Circuit., where growing FOC, 0,15 hes been experienced. Indeed it hex been hie god fortnre ttirbughbitt his ministry to I, are his Cir'nite better then be found them, owing to the warn hearted service of the Methodist folk. Mr. Ilecksct tells •1 that it ix a joy to him to knov that hie lot will soon be cast In the midst cf a united and prorperous Circuit. He i• • strainer to the Ishii rpoul dint riot, hot spent three yearn of his early miniatry In Yorkshire and three years of his later misixtry in Cheshi.e.</p>
        <p>NEW MINISTER bOlt BOLD-STREET CHI'IICII. The Rev. Hugh Williamvon, who has been appointed to the Warrington Wealeyan Circuit, with charge of Bold-etreet Church, wee emerged as candidate for the Wesleyan ministry in 1902 and week forthwith sent aro a non-cdleg ate to the Sutton (Surrey) Circuit for one year. The following tso years were spent at Headingley College. Since leaving there Ike has @Tent three years in the Ticehurst Circuit and three years in the Hexharu Circuit.</p>
