      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-05_WidnesExaminer_art0057" n="art0057">
        <head>St. John's Church Guild</head>
        <p>St. John's Church Guild</p>
        <p>On Saturday the membera of St. John'aChnrch to the number of about twenty bad an enjoyable after- noon's ramble to Croft. Startrng from the car terrain., Manchester-road, at 3 p.m. the party proceeded by way of Orford Village and Houghton Grim, On arrival at Croft the company had tea at 'l. Olds Croft Tea- room.; and later made the journey homewards by way of Winwick, re•ching Warrington at 0-30 p.m. Favoured with ideal weather for leisurely rambling by field and wood, tLe party thoroughly enjoyed themselvea.</p>
