      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-05_WidnesExaminer_art0058" n="art0058">
        <head>Sankey Bridges Wesley Guild.</head>
        <p>Sankey Bridges Wesley Guild.</p>
        <p>Th. monthly devotional meeting of the guild was I held on Monday. The members hid • new and pleasant experience, for instead of meeting in the guild room, i they gathered on the lawn at Ssokey list!, the residence I of the Rev. Joseph Howard. The attendance numbered shout sixty, which speaks well for the future success of the open.air devotional meetings. The Ite•. F. IV. liernick, M.A., gnus on excellent address strongly urging everyone to feel their own responsibility and to do some definite work for the church. Several if the members rifterwsrds testified to the great benefit they had received from the Wesley truild, and paid tribute to the ministry of Mr. Kernick, expressing their sorrow at his approaching depsrture to Illxcia.urn. A vote of than's wits pissed to Mr. Howard for his kind ness in allowing the guild to meet on his lawn. Mr. Howard suitably replied and gsve a few reminiscences of his early lit.</p>
