        <p>On Sunday reining the Rev. W. Reid, preached at St. John's from Ephesians i., 10, " 'co gather together In one all things in Christ." Mr. Reid compered the teschings of Calvinism lased upon the interpretation it placed on Scripture, with those of St. Pool, the writer of the epistle, and proceealed to show that it wen inconeistr at with the trend of the whole doctrine of the apostle, as well RS inconsistent with the revelation of Goli.given try Christ, to argue that he ',went that by the decree of bits] some men are foreordained to ever- lasting death, or that in consequence of en arbitrary election, a men knowing within, of God'. redemptive power is still cue of the elect. The eternal Son pro. coaled the preacher, 1.111 the elect, the uhosen ne, in , whom the everiesting Father rot the i tool humanity whom he destined for that tern, glorioos gunship, and to be re.boro of the Spirit of the chosen one was to belong Sr the elect race, of which lie was the founder and bead.</p>
