        <p>! - been purchased for building purp-ses ...rid it is being •Uractively laid out under the title of the M ,unt Pleasant Estate. The land is on the Vicarage side of the Liverpo 1 highway and is ab sat four minutes walk from the Cheshire Lines.statio fro n which station there run 39 trains to and from Warringtea to Sankey pr day. The estate occupies an elevated polition ani commands a delightful prospect of the surrounding county. There meanders at the foot if the land a heautifnlly clear wean], in which both eels and Bounders have been caught. The land having a good fall permit,. , f perfect drainage. The development of the I alaie will be in sec .rd- once with the most modern ideals. The villas to be built up n it will he well net back front the road, and cow that tl e ri ad has Inert tar-sprayed and the dust fiend has been fail, the conditions are all that one could a i.h. Villas are being erected at rents ranging from £3l) to £2O per annum. Of recent years the taste and art of building have undergone a great change f.,r the liter, 80 that a famine writer'e description of the Englishman's dwellings as '' so many brick b am with elate ' is no huger justified. Inst, al of miles of endless streets, it itheut a break in architecture, the idealists are providing ea with houses which vary in their gicturesqu.meas and wham environment maken for greeter comfort, more open spaces, and more attractive exterior.. In the tto villas which have already been erectrel at Mount Pleasant the housewife has 6-en carefully considered arid her comforts and conveni- ence catered for. A rood, spacious hall, 121 t. wide, • . .</p>
