      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1911-08-05_WidnesExaminer_art0124" n="art0124">
        <head>Guild Workers Visit, Frodsham.</head>
        <p>Guild Workers Visit, Frodsham.</p>
        <p>On Saturdaythe hat of the series'of gar len pirties for Wart-114bn Guild of Help workers was held at Frodeharn on the invitation of Mr. and Mrs. W. N. Hutchings. The helpers for the Bewsey, Whitecrosa, and St. Austin's Wards aseembled in the charming at-curds of " Hillsborough," and were glad to Atelier on the shaded lawn from the blazing sun. After tea • short meeting of the group took place, when the toll 'wing officers spoke, viz . Meters. B. S. Townroe. W. Webster and A. C. Binks. CBOO3 Blogg &amp;leo made a happy speech, in which be commended the objects of the Guild. Cordial thanks were given to Hr. and Mrs. Hutchings. Druring the afternoon, the guests competed for prizes in clock-golf and ladder- golf. A number of Frodatam residents were *h..° present.</p>
